# What holds: a place read and changed stands twice, a choice is a coproduct of its arms, a call into a family is a
# choice between its members.

# `bump` reads the count at the path it is handed and writes the next one there: one place, read and changed, so it
# stands on both sides. The path is a parameter of the route, which no code decides.
route counter.bump
step bump/read_count
step bump/write_count

line entry > bump call
line Disk(bump.path) > bump/read_count own
line bump/read_count > bump back                         # the count, of no type of the code's, goes on to bump (#101)
line bump/write_count > Disk(bump.path) own

side entry left
side Disk(bump.path) both

# `pick` makes its Table in one of two arms: the value is made by the choice, and `show` takes it after.
route counter.pick
choice pick/?1
step pick/?1/load_csv
step pick/?1/load_csv/Table()
step pick/?1/load_json
step pick/?1/load_json/Table()
step pick/show

line entry > pick call
line Disk(pick.path) > pick/?1/load_csv own
line Disk(pick.path) > pick/?1/load_json own
line pick/?1/load_csv/Table() > Table@pick/?1/load_csv/Table() value
line Table@pick/?1/load_csv/Table() > pick/?1/load_csv value
line pick/?1/load_csv > Table·t@pick/?1 value
line pick/?1/load_json/Table() > Table@pick/?1/load_json/Table() value
line Table@pick/?1/load_json/Table() > pick/?1/load_json value
line pick/?1/load_json > Table·t@pick/?1 value
line Table·t@pick/?1 > pick/show value
line pick/show > Screen own

home Table@pick/?1/load_csv/Table() pick/?1/load_csv
home Table@pick/?1/load_json/Table() pick/?1/load_json
home Table·t@pick/?1 pick

side entry left
side Disk(pick.path) left
side Screen right

# `draw_all` calls `draw` on each Shape it is handed: the loop is a step of its own, which takes the shapes and gives
# each `s` (#103), and the call runs one of the overrides on it, a choice between them.
route counter.draw_all
step draw_all/for s in shapes
step draw_all/Shape.draw
step draw_all/Shape.draw/Circle.draw
step draw_all/Shape.draw/Square.draw

line entry > draw_all call
line Shape·shapes > draw_all value
line Shape·shapes > draw_all/for s in shapes value
line draw_all/for s in shapes > Shape·s@draw_all/for s in shapes value
line Shape·s@draw_all/for s in shapes > draw_all/Shape.draw value
line Shape·s@draw_all/for s in shapes > draw_all/Shape.draw/Circle.draw value
line Shape·s@draw_all/for s in shapes > draw_all/Shape.draw/Square.draw value
line draw_all/Shape.draw/Circle.draw > draw_all/Shape.draw back
line draw_all/Shape.draw/Square.draw > draw_all/Shape.draw back
line draw_all/Shape.draw > draw_all back
line draw_all > Screen own

home Shape·shapes draw_all
home Shape·s@draw_all/for s in shapes draw_all

side entry left
side Screen right
